WEBVTT

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.690
I had a feeling it was you.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.420
Why haven't you run?

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.880
As long as Tiffa's aboard that ship, I'm not going anywhere.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:00.220
There's nothing you can do. You can't take away her pain.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:04.430
You guys keep chasing her around! Just leave her alone!

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.810
Tiffa didn't ask for that kind of power!

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:23.870
My captive princess, I've come for you.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:25.960
I...

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.620
I love Tiffa!

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.210
I love you. So badly that I want to kill you.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:55.900
After War

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:55.900
GUNDAM

00:01:55.900 --> 00:02:03.410
<b>The dream I'd nearly forgotten is beginning to stir,</b>

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:06.370
<b>little by little</b>

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:10.920
<b>filling in the gaps in my heart.</b>

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:18.300
<b>The instant my frozen memories begin to awaken,</b>

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:27.810
<b>my only wish is for the future that is about to begin.</b>

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.350
<b>I'll reach out with both hands</b>

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:35.360
<b>and embrace that dream I once had.</b>

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.990
<b>I want to go on believing</b>

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:42.910
<b>without ever letting go or giving up.</b>

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:46.540
<b>Until the day comes when I grab hold....</b>

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.420
<b>...of that dream I once had,</b>

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.960
<b>I want to keep chasing after it</b>

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:59.800
<b>without ever forgetting my hopes and dreams.</b>

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:10.560
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:10.560
<b>"This Operation Is a Race Against the Clock!"</b>

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.610
Where are you going?

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.860
Isn't it obvious? Back to the ship.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:22.990
Captain!

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.700
So this is where you went! There's a problem!

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:26.830
Is it Tiffa?

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:30.160
Her condition has taken a sudden turn.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.040
I-It's what?!

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:42.050
I don't know what's causing it, but her nerve tissue has started to collapse.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.470
At this rate, she has about a week.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.720
Y-You can't be serious!

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.770
With the proper facilities, I could probably do something...

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.310
But where can we find such a place?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.020
No. I know a place.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.110
You want us to hit that Alternative Company lab again?!

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.580
He says it like it's nothing.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:09.540
Right?

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.290
I don't know the situation, so I couldn't say.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.250
This operation is a race against the clock!

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.460
Our attack target is the Alternative Company's medical facility.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.050
I want to capture it intact.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.340
Just a second there, Jamil.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:28.050
I still haven't decided if I'm on board with this job.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.470
You'll be paid well for your time.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.230
Sweet! Then I'm in!

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.060
Suit yourself.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.730
The lab's already been attacked once.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.650
Their security's going to be a lot heavier than before.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:46.660
Isn't it a wee bit optimistic to think we can just waltz in there?

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.580
I'm aware of the risk. However-

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:53.750
If we don't go, that girl will die. Is that it?

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.540
That's what I don't get, though.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.960
We have our own misgivings about that, sir.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:03.670
We have always acted with absolute faith in you, Captain.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:06.760
But there are just too many unanswered questions here.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:12.220
Why are you so fixated on that Tiffa Adill girl?

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:17.190
Is there something about her that makes her worth our lives?

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.400
Please don't say it's about love.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:26.530
Anyway, whether or not I cancel this gig depends on your answer.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:28.360
Yeah, same here.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:31.330
Seriously, you always follow his lead.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:32.700
Bite me!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.920
I have bad news, Jamil.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:43.380
She can't be...

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.920
She can. Her condition is worsening, and at an accelerating rate.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.180
At this rate, she won't last two days, much less a week.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.640
Understood.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.700
It was fifteen years ago.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:18.500
Fifteen years ago, I fought in the war as a soldier for the U.N.E...

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.710
As the pilot of the Mobile Suit Gundam.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.590
The Gundam's pilot?!

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:36.310
I was the one who caused the tragedy that day.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:42.190
There once was a war.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:53.570
A conflict that arose from a single colony's independence movement...

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.540
...grew into a worst-case scenario, total war between the colonies and Earth.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:03.500
Eight months after the fighting reached a stalemate,

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.420
the colonies decided to risk gunboat diplomacy.

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:12.300
Threatening a colony drop operation that would cause massive damage to the Earth,

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.680
they demanded the U.N.E.'s surrender.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:19.890
In response, the United Nations Earth Forces sent in their ultimate secret weapon,

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:24.940
the Mobile Suit Gundam, prepared to fight to the bitter end.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:31.360
And I, fifteen years younger, was the one controlling the Gundam GX-9900 that day.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.700
Controlling the unmanned Bit mobile suits...

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.620
...that were fielded for the colony intercept operation...

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.630
...required the powers of a Newtype such as myself.

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:39.890
However, that one volley...

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:43.480
...was the trigger that set off the greatest tragedy in human history.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:48.520
Eager for victory, the S.R.A. went through with their operation.

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:53.240
The U.F.E. held their ground and fought back.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:57.320
The fighting became bogged down, and then...

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.040
You know the rest.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:10.290
The fighting intensified, and all was lost.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:15.260
We Newtypes were pressed into service as tools of war, and most of us died.

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:21.640
So the rumors that there were soldiers with superpowers in the war are true.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.270
Captain, do you still have your powers?

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:29.060
No. If I try too hard to use them, I only get a blinding headache.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:34.190
Oh, so that Tiffa girl is one of those Newtypes.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:39.660
There's a strong enough possibility. That's why I want to protect her.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.330
And not just Tiffa.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.580
If there are others out there with similar powers,

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:48.120
I intend to protect them, whatever the cost.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:53.210
That is the reason that I am so "fixated" on Tiffa Adill.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:55.760
Does that answer your questions?

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:56.550
Yes, sir.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.930
Captain, I'll take the helm.

00:09:58.970 --> 00:09:59.930
Thanks.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:06.890
Most of that went over my head, but I guess I'm okay with this.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:09.140
I appreciate that.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.770
Sorry, but I'm out.

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:13.980
I'm quitting, too.

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:19.700
I hate it when people buy into that kind of thinking.

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:23.370
I don't like it, either. That stuff's too heavy for me.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:27.500
I expected as much. I won't try to stop you.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.460
You will be paid through today as per your contracts.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.290
I guess that's our cue to leave, then!

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:34.420
Let's pack our stuff.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:35.590
You bet.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.380
That's the problem with freelancers...

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:41.840
And what about you?

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:47.100
I am in your debt for saving me, so please let me assist you.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:48.600
That's a relief!

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:51.520
But what do we do, Captain?

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:54.020
Without those two, we're short on firepower.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.370
What do you think you're doing?

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:07.160
If you want us to help you escape, ask somebody else.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:10.250
It's not that! I want you to help Jamil!

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:14.380
Oh, I get it. You heard what he said on the bridge.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:17.090
Sorry, we don't have time to play with kids right now.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.960
Hey, wait!

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.930
Stand aside if you don't want to get hurt.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.050
I'm begging you, work with-

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.720
Quit bothering me.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:36.900
P-Please...

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:38.480
Give it a rest!

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.410
I told you you'd get hurt.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:57.420
I was stupid to even ask.

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:05.300
He gave me the stink-eye. Learn how the world works, kid.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:09.720
Learn how the world works, huh? Everybody's like that when they're a kid.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:14.190
You can't differentiate between what you want to do and what you can do.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.560
Sometimes you feel like you can change the world by yourself,

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:20.190
and sometimes you get mad at how helpless you are.

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:22.650
That's what it means to be a kid.

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:25.530
I'm surprised you're taking his side.

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:29.330
Hardly. That means that adults can't deal with them.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:37.790
That little bastard did give me the stink-eye, though...

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:41.260
"Farewell, o youth"... Or something like that.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:10.370
I'd rather that you didn't interrupt my reading.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:14.710
I'll be outside. Call me when you're done.

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.600
Tiffa, I'm sorry.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:39.520
You're in this mess because I'm such an idiot.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:45.320
I had him all wrong.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:50.450
I assumed that that Jamil guy was a bad person.

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.080
But nothing could have been further from the truth.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:58.790
This whole time, he's cared about you way more than I have.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:04.210
I kinda feel ashamed of myself now.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:10.050
You'll have to cut it short. Someone's coming.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:15.270
I'll be back, so don't die on me. Don't you dare die, you hear?

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.280
He'll be back, huh?

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:29.610
I only hope she lasts that long.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:53.930
A red Vulture Sign signifies a request for assistance.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:15:00.270
Short on firepower, Jamil has put out a request for help to his fellow Vultures.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.860
Been a long time, Jamil!

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:09.990
Rosso Aramant, thank you for helping!

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.490
I'll help, so make sure you throw in a little something for my trouble!

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:22.500
I owe you one, Jamil. I've been waiting for a chance to repay you.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:25.250
I'm glad you hear you say that, Grits Joe.

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:30.380
Still running solo, I see.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:35.600
If we pull this off, how about teaming up with me? On a personal basis.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:38.770
I'll consider it, Rosa Intenso.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:42.940
And you're as good a liar as ever. But I'll let it go.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.900
Our Captain sure is impressive.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.400
Call it personal magnetism.

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:53.280
With this many Vultures, we should be able to manage, Captain.

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:56.780
All right, let's begin the briefing.

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:09.630
First, we will split into two groups and begin a cannon bombardment.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:13.260
Five minutes later, we will launch all our mobile suits...

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:15.140
...and rendezvous in front of the lab.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.850
We will then attempt a direct charge.

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.010
Oh, I get it.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:22.100
We make them think we're attacking from two directions.

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:24.560
You want to get them to divide their forces.

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:25.650
Correct.

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:30.650
Make certain that your cannon fire lands just short of the lab compound.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.820
However, we need to be careful to keep them from realizing...

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.620
...that it is a diversion.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:44.330
They will come straight at us.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.960
Are you certain?

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:49.250
You doubt our abilities?

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.210
I merely thought-

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:55.130
I don't blame you. But you'll see soon enough.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:00.180
They'll send out the GX?

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:03.890
That's right. Given Tiffa's condition, time is of the essence.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:07.690
The operation will commence at Moonrise.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:10.070
We'll finish them off in one stroke with the Satellite Cannon.

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:11.690
But who will pilot it?

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:13.740
That Garrod boy?

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:16.490
No. I'll go out.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:32.090
I see. They intend to use the Moon's power, do they?

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:33.880
What are you talking about?

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:36.800
I'd like to borrow a few men.

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:40.930
I'm going to get the drop on them.

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:43.520
Understood, Brother.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:52.610
We'll hit them before the Moon comes out.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:19.630
Shouldn't we be working on that mobile armor, too?

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:21.140
He said he'd do it himself.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:22.470
Oh.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.770
Fine with me, that's less work for us.

00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:33.820
Okay, that's everything. We'll let the Chief handle the rest.

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:49.460
What do you think you're doing?

00:18:55.960 --> 00:19:00.800
Oh, it's just a kid... Go on, beat it! Stupid punk...

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:04.600
What's the big idea?!

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:08.060
That hurt!

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:11.100
That does it, you twerp! Now I'm mad!

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:12.730
You little punk!

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:16.150
You're the punk, punk!

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:17.440
Bastard!

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:18.190
Chief!

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:19.820
You bastard!

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:22.820
Ow ow ow ow ow!

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.830
I was wondering you who were. So you're Gundam Boy, huh?

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:32.080
A kid like you doesn't get to call people "boy"!

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:34.290
Shut your mouth, you moron.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:38.000
Watch your tone!

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:43.470
This here's Kid Salsamille! He's in charge of all us mechanics!

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:47.890
Nice to meet'cha. I'm a boy genius.

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:49.890
What's all the commotion?

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:52.890
Hey, Jamil. Look what we have here.

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:55.400
You!

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:03.030
I'm begging you! Please lend me the Gundam!

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:09.040
I want to fight to help Tiffa! No, to help people like Tiffa!

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:10.750
You...

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.540
I heard your story earlier.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:16.920
I'll pilot the GX.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:21.880
Wait, is it cured, Jamil? Your cockpit phobia, I mean.

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:26.340
Sorry.

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:28.760
Cockpit phobia?

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:32.230
Don't say that! I have PTSD.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:35.690
Oh, I didn't know... Then that's all the more reason for me to-

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:38.020
What's going on?

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:47.320
What was that?!

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:56.210
Now, behold the true form of my Gundam Ashtaron!

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.050
What the...? That thing was also a Gundam?

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:11.600
Tiffa!

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:19.810
My princess fair, I shall save you.

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:32.240
Stop that! She mustn't be moved!

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:43.800
Tiffa!

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.470
Mobile suit squad detected dead ahead!

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:56.890
It worked perfectly, Brother.

00:21:57.020 --> 00:22:02.610
That's my little brother. All that's left now is to finish them.

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:21.420
That looks bad!

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:26.510
Twilight, eh? This might be the ideal time for them to die.

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:32.430
Go to hell before you get a chance to see the Moon.

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:51.070
<b>Can I find the words to tell you</b>

00:22:48.020 --> 00:22:53.410
The Freeden is in peril when it comes under brutal attack by the mysterious Frost Brothers.

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:56.450
<b>How I live between the walls of steel and stone</b>

00:22:53.410 --> 00:22:56.370
Plus, as part of Von's plan to wipe out the Vultures,

00:22:56.370 --> 00:23:00.290
he has the mobile armor Grandeene fire on them repeatedly.

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:04.290
<b>How I close my eyes to find some kind of rapture</b>

00:23:00.290 --> 00:23:03.520
Jamil, with help from Tiffa and Garrod,

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:05.420
risks everything in a desperate gamble.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:10.630
<b>In a world where you can feel so all alone</b>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:17.640
<b>Inside I'm full of light and laughter</b>

00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:21.520
<b>There's a flame that burns in me</b>

00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:22.480
<b>(I need a way)</b>

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:26.570
<b>(I need a way) I need a way to set it free</b>

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:31.490
<b>When you find love in your heart</b>

00:23:31.490 --> 00:23:33.620
<b>(The human touch)</b>

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:37.660
<b>You can believe from the start</b>

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:39.660
<b>(From the start)</b>

00:23:40.580 --> 00:23:42.790
<b>Dreams they come true</b>

00:23:42.790 --> 00:23:44.170
<b>(They come true)</b>

